A||N||18||bocefas||Rear window Defrost install||||1||
Z||000000||bocefas||10-29-2001||09:58 PM||||Has anyone ever bothered to swap out a standard rear window for one with the elec. defroster?  I have a defrost window in a parts car and wanted to swap it into my '86 GT.  Any info would be helpful...It looks like a simple thing to do, but I thought I'd ask before i (^(&ed up both cars trying it!||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||10-30-2001||12:48 AM||||It is not as simple as you may think.......polyurethane all the way around. I use a heated blade made for removing windshields to remove the rear windows but it is still quite a chore. You can find window removal tools at most parts stores.<P>Other than that, just remove and replace. Then run the wiring from the dash to the rear window defrost connector at the rear window and you are done.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.whgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>West Highland Graphics & Design</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||U Wanna Race||10-30-2001||01:53 AM||||Why?  It is pointless to have a rear defogger in a fiero.  The heat from the engine is more than enough to keep your window fog-free.||||reg||1
Z||000003||bocefas||10-30-2001||05:53 AM||||If it was "pointless" to have one, I can't imagine GM would have offered one...actually the heat from the engine seems to cause the initial fogging during the spring and fall, and is no where hot enough to melt ice off the window, at least not quickly, in the winter.  My 5:30 AM departure time for work doesn't help things either, my windows are always frosted over, and I'm in no mood to scrape, I just want to be able to start it 5 minutes early and take off.  I'm going to do it, I'll let you know how it turns out, pass or fail.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroFanaticus2||10-30-2001||07:09 AM||||My rear window has never fogged up, no rear defroster either.||||reg||1
Z||000005||falconhulk||10-30-2001||07:38 AM||||Had ice on every part of the car yesterday morning.  Rear window was the fist thing to clear up without a defogger.  The engine is plenty hot enough to melt ice.||||reg||1
Z||000006||PBJ||10-30-2001||09:25 AM||||I agree it is pointless. All the fieros I have owned have had rear deff and have never once turned one on. The heat of the engine clears the fog in no time. Have you ever touched the rear glass after 5 min of driving or how about after 15 min of city driving, you cant even keep your hand on it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||10-30-2001||09:32 AM||||Who cares if it's pointless?  If the bocefas wants it and has the parts, either help him with info or leave it alone.  tgowens is the only person to constructively respond to this thread so far.  And that's all I have to say.||||reg||13
Z||000008||FieroJoe||10-30-2001||10:30 AM||||If you havent set windshields or rear glass before, you might want to see what a local glass shop would ding ya for them to do it.  They already have all the tools to remove your defogger window and your standard one out of your GT.  They will also set it properly, with a 2 part urethane adhesive, and will probably check to make sure there isnt any leaks.  The leak testing is pretty cool, they set a little box inside the car, have you (carefully) shut all your doors with windows rolled up and sunroof closed, and then they drag another little probe around the edge of the glass and it will beep if a signal gets through to the box on my inside.  He also checked my sunroof and now I know where its leaking from.<P>also, you'll probably find that the main power feed for the defogger control box comes from the white power distribution center under the corner of the dash, near where the left front speaker is.  Everything should be plug and play, but Im not speaking from experience either.<P>I think that the timer box is bolted to one of the sides of the steering column.<p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||10-30-2001||04:09 PM||||im with most others here. the engine heat defrosts 10 times faster than any window defroster ever will. I used the switch for my driving lites. Pontiac wasnt as dumb on that as everyone thinks, they sold it (at a profit im sure) on probably most of them. Probably made them a few million extra bucks. <P>by the way, what if you break either or both taking them out (happens more than not) just a thought <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Dumba$$||10-30-2001||05:48 PM||||you wouldnt be snagging that out of the 87 gt you wanna trade me is it?<BR>not that it really matters<P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE <BR>98 acura cl 3.0<P>4.9 caddy engine for sale 30,000 miles complete with bubba joes mounts!!  $750||||reg||1
Z||000011||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-30-2001||06:39 PM||||I have the factory rear defrost in my fiero and I tend to use it a LOT during the winters here in Canada..  Might be ok to not have one in the warmer US states, but it sure comes in handy in colder areas.   And yes.. it does make a difference having one.. and the engine heat dont clean my window completely (at least for the first few miles of driving)<P>Installation should not be a problem, I would also suggest to remove your spare one carefully then to pay a windshield shop to install it properly for you.. but completely up to you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||bocefas||10-30-2001||08:20 PM||||Rich, No, although that GT has one in it, I have an 85 coupe with one in it that's pretty much stripped, so I thought I'd take that out before I pay my final respects to it...Thanks you for the defense Formula88...and I do appreciate everyones input.  My GT is loaded except for that, and I have one, so why not???  It didn't have Power Mirrors, which I think are more pointless than the defroster, but I added those, and I am in the process of adding the factory Sub, so the defroster is the only thing left except for a lumbar seat, but I can't find one of those (In Grey if anyone has one)...if I can find one I'll add it too...this car has been in my family since new and only has 69,000 miles on it, and I want to keep it around, so I figure why not give it all of the amenities...||||reg||1
