Z||000018||Cliff Pennock||11-05-2001||08:00 PM||||I have a defroster on my rear window and it helps <B>a lot</B>. Not only for getting rid of ice quicker, but imagine what happens when the rear window is only heated from the outside: your glass will be a lot warmer on the outside than on the inside which means that condensation will leave form on the inside. The condensation will eventually evaporate, but it will a whole lot of crap on your window. Since the defroster is on the inside, the inside of the window will heat up slightly faster than on the outside: no condensation.<P>But the easiest way to get a defroster is to simply buy one of those you can simply stick on the inside of your window. You'll be done in 30 minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Cliff Pennock (edited 11-05-2001).]||||reg||1
